# macOS
.DS_Store

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Next.js app in web/
#
# node_modules alone is over 11,000 files. Without this, tools that show a file
# count — Git Graph, the VS Code SCM panel — report the whole dependency tree as
# pending changes, which is where "10k files changed" comes from. Listed here at
# the root rather than only in web/.gitignore so there is one obvious place to
# look.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.next/
next-env.d.ts
*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets: the Supabase URL and anon key for a real project.
.env.local
.env*.local

.env.example
.env*.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The old static site's member register — NEVER commit this.
#
# static-site/data/members.json holds every member's phone number as a
# PBKDF2-SHA256 hash. "Hashed" is not the same as safe here, and the reason is
# the size of the input: a Japanese mobile is 0[789]0 plus eight digits, about
# 3x10^8 possibilities. That is small enough to try all of them.
#
# Worse, the file uses ONE SHARED SALT for all 28 members, so a single pass over
# those 300 million candidates recovers every number at once rather than one at
# a time. On a single GPU that is hours, not years — and this repository is
# public.
#
# The file is kept outside the repository, next to the original static site. The
# Next.js app does not use it: numbers live in Supabase, in a table `anon` has no
# grant on at all.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
static-site/data/
